From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:04:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the DS game picker

Switches the ARM9 to 134 MHz in DSi mode, then indexes every IWAD and
mod (PWAD) in NitroFS and on the SD card in a picker on the bottom
screen console that shows each game's title picture, runs mods on a
matching IWAD, shows a loading screen and keeps config and saves in
/data/doom/<wad name>/. A title picture is only drawn when it is a patch with all
of its columns inside the lump, picker lines are cut to one row so a tap
picks the game it is on. The picker sleeps while the lid is closed and
exits on the DSi power button or L+R+START+SELECT. Doom then runs in a
thread with a 64 KiB stack in main RAM: DTCM is mostly taken by the
light tables, and Doom's deepest recursion grows with the size of a map.
Also the doomgeneric interface: timing from the calico tick counter.
